WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.823
The payouts table keeps each amount in euros, like 40.00.

2
00:00:06.823 --> 00:00:12.972
You want a column of whole cents instead, amount_minor, like every other money field.

3
00:00:12.972 --> 00:00:17.312
Six instances of the payout service use this column all day.

4
00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:25.815
A deploy replaces them one at a time, so for a few minutes old code and new code run side by side against the same table.

5
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:34.581
Rename and convert the column in one migration, and the moment it runs, every old instance fails: column amount does not exist.

6
00:00:34.581 --> 00:00:37.960
Stopping the service first means downtime instead.

7
00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.012
Instead, change it in phases.

8
00:00:40.012 --> 00:00:43.257
Each phase works with the code on both sides of it.

9
00:00:43.433 --> 00:00:47.328
First, expand: add amount_minor as a new, empty column.

10
00:00:47.328 --> 00:00:52.001
It allows NULL, so old inserts that never mention it keep working.

11
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:57.694
Then deploy v2, which writes both columns in one statement but still reads amount.

12
00:00:57.694 --> 00:01:02.987
Until the rollout ends, a v1 instance can still add a row with no amount_minor.

13
00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:12.389
Once the last v1 instance is gone, a backfill job fills every NULL with amount times a hundred, a few thousand rows per transaction.

14
00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:15.202
Deploy v3, which reads amount_minor.

15
00:01:15.202 --> 00:01:20.412
For a while it also reads amount and logs any row where the two disagree.

16
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:25.108
Then v4 writes only amount_minor, and nothing reads amount any more.

17
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:29.637
Last, contract: once no running version mentions amount, drop it.

18
00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:37.453
One rename became several deploys, and at no point did a running version see a schema it couldn't use.
